{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK4hpJC2pVsN8uqFHm7z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the bug with a one-line change at `django/db/models/sql/compiler.py:35`, the regex that `get_order_by()` uses to strip the ordering from each clause:\n\n```python\nself.ordering_parts = re.compile(r'(.*)\\s(ASC|DESC)(.*)', re.MULTILINE | re.DOTALL)\n```\n\nBefore, `.` in the regex didn't match newlines, so the captured text was only the last line of a multiline RawSQL clause. Two clauses ending in the same line, like `else null end` in your example, looked like duplicates and the second was dropped. With `re.DOTALL`, `.` matches newlines too, so the full SQL is captured and compared. This also covers `\\r\\n` line endings, which your suggestion to split on `\\n` would have missed.\n\nThe `expressions`, `ordering` and `queries` test modules pass (513 tests). I didn't run your three-clause query or write a new test for the multiline case, so the fix isn't directly tested on it yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":228,"cache_read_input_tokens":19530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":228},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d056a84a-ae1b-4b4e-93bd-74bc7990ef64","uuid":"eaf5801d-1ee2-4b31-ad58-ab5ab27ec12c","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:23:40.886Z","request_id":"req_011ChK4hp9kqqZRG2cQ3D6Me"}
